---

## [2.0.0] — 2026-05

### Added

- Instrumentation Manager: 19 trackers across Spatial (5), Device (10), XR (4) categories
- Instrumentation Manager: auto-assign Camera.main to UserPostureComponent.headTransform and EyeTrackingComponent.cam on add
- Instrumentation Manager: auto-fill ExperienceInfoComponent.appVersion from Application.version and targetHardware from SystemInfo.deviceModel via SerializedObject delayCall
- Instrumentation Manager: Scene Health Check (XROrigin TrackingOriginMode warning; XRInputModalityManager missing hand prefab warning)
- Instrumentation Manager: preAddHint / postAddHint per-tracker guidance copy in Trackers tab
- Instrumentation Manager: 3-tier device tracker fallback (GossipManager -> _playerObject -> "Gossip Device Trackers" host)
- Instrumentation Manager: color-coded footer status bar (objects / trackers / permissions counts)
- Instrumentation Manager: Done button cancel-safe (SaveCurrentModifiedScenesIfUserWantsTo return value checked)
- GossipBuildPreprocessor: auto-disables EnableDebug before every build (IPreprocessBuildWithReport)
- GossipUninstaller: clears Library/PackageCache/com.gossip.core@* after Client.Remove()
- AudioVolumeTrackerComponent: configurable dB normalisation range via public fields dbMin (default -80f) and dbMax (default 0f)
- AudioReactionTrackerComponent: 8 tunable [SerializeField] parameters — scoreWeightEnergy/Voice/Movement, signalThresholdEnergy/Voice/Movement, rmsNormCeiling, movementSpeedCeiling
- EyeTrackingComponent: configurable head-fallback multipliers (headFallbackCooldownMultiplier = 1.5f, headFallbackThresholdMultiplier = 2.5f)
- ConnectivityMonitorComponent: configurable speed test timeout via public int speedTestTimeoutSeconds (default 5)
- HeatmapSceneAutoCapture: configurable captureDelay (default 0.5f) and cameraHeight (default 100f) as [SerializeField] fields
- TextNarrationCoverageTracker: sdk_version now uses Application.version dynamically

### Fixed

- AudioReactionTrackerComponent: EventSeverity computed from real microphone RMS; MovementIntensity from normalised head velocity (were hardcoded 0.6 / 0.4)
- AudioReactionTrackerComponent: trackedTransform auto-assigned in Start() via Camera.main?.transform fallback; TriggerSnippet() null guard added
- HandControllerTrackingComponent: removed fabricated Send("left", Quaternion.identity) from Start() — first real data arrives from periodic Update() sampler
- MistakeReporter: replaced silent GossipManager fallback with Debug.LogError + disabled = true; all data paths guarded with if (disabled) return
- PlatformMonitorComponent: ControllersLatency and AmountDevicesInGame marked with TODO comments (not yet implemented)
- Instrumentation Manager: Unity overloaded null check enforced for tracker component cache — prevents ArgumentException on stale destroyed-object references
- Instrumentation Manager: AutoDetectPlayer and AutoAddTrackers now run on every Open() call, not only on cold domain-reload start

---

## [1.1.1] - 2026-05-24
### Fixed
- **EyeTrackingTracker.cs** and **InputUsageTracker.cs**: Removed invalid `[SerializeField]` attributes from `EntityData` auto-properties. `[SerializeField]` only works on instance fields, not auto-properties — Unity silently ignored them, causing `EntityData` values to never serialize correctly.
- **Gossip.cs**: `EyeTrackingTracker` and `InputUsageTracker` were missing from the `RunResendLoopAsync` resend worker list. Both trackers now share the same automatic retry resilience as all other trackers.

---

## [1.0.0] - 2026-02-02
### Added
- Initial public release of the Gossip Analytics Unity SDK.
- Core SDK runtime via `GossipManager`.
- Settings asset workflow (`GossipAnalyticsSettings`) for environment configuration (Dev/Beta/Production).
- OpenXR-first support via `XR Bootstrap`.
- Public integration documentation:
  - `README.md`
  - `docs/trackers.md`
- Trackers (public reference): accessories, ads, audio reaction/volume, avatar, battery, connectivity, difficulty, distance, experience info, eye tracking, hand controller, input usage, interaction, memory/performance, mistakes, multiplayer, passthrough, pause, peripherals, platform, playable area, position, reality mode, rotation/velocity, server status, session, user balance, user posture, custom user events.

### Changed
- N/A

### Fixed
- N/A
